// Tymora's Champion

@100 = ~Tymora's Champion~
@101 = ~Tymora's Champion~
@102 = ~TYMORA'S CHAMPION: Every halfling knows a lucky one: the cousin who fell off the roof onto a haycart, the uncle who won the farm at cards. Tymora's Champion is that cousin, grown up and sworn to the Lady. Arrows miss by a whisker, blades turn on a buckle, and when death finally comes calling, Tymora rolls the dice one more time.

Advantages:
– Luck: +1 at levels 1, 10, 20, 30 and 40.
– Lucky Dodge: +1 AC for every point of the Champion's own Luck.
– Fortune's Path: +1 movement for every point of the Champion's own Luck.
– +1 to all saves at Luck 1 and 2, +2 at Luck 3 and 4, and +3 at Luck 5.
– May use Lady's Favour once per day at level 1, plus once more at levels 6, 11, 16 and every 5 levels after.
  LADY'S FAVOUR: +3 Luck for 1 turn, with the matching AC, movement and save bonuses.
– From level 10: Tymora Smiles. Once a day, if the Champion falls below 10% of its hit points, it is instantly healed to about half.
– May reach grandmastery in all its weapons.

Disadvantages:
– May wear armour up to splint mail.
– May only use bucklers and small shields.
– May only use short swords, flails and morning stars, maces, clubs, daggers, darts, slings and short bows.
– Must be a chaotic good halfling.~

@110 = ~Luck of the Lady~
@111 = ~The Lady's favour grows as Tymora's Champion does: +1 Luck, +1 AC and +1 movement at levels 1, 10, 20, 30 and 40, with better saves as the Luck builds.~

@120 = ~Lady's Favour~
@121 = ~Lady's Favour

For 1 turn, the Champion gains +3 Luck, +3 AC, +3 movement and better saves. Using it again while it is still running starts the turn afresh.~
@122 = ~Lady's Favour~

@130 = ~Tymora Smiles~
@131 = ~Tymora Smiles

Once a day, when the Champion falls below 10% of its hit points, Tymora steps in and heals it to about half. It recovers one game day after it last fired.~
@132 = ~Tymora smiles!~

@140 = ~Fortune's Turn~
@141 = ~Fortune's Turn

For 1 turn, the Champion gains +2 to all saves, and enemies within 30 feet suffer -2 Luck. Does not stack with Fortune's Wheel.~

@145 = ~Fortune's Wheel~
@146 = ~Fortune's Wheel

For 1 turn, the Champion gains +4 to all saves, and enemies within 30 feet suffer -3 Luck. Replaces Fortune's Turn if it is running.~

@150 = ~Tymora's Blessing~
@151 = ~Tymora's Blessing

The Champion and its allies nearby gain +3 Luck for 1 turn. This Luck does not raise the Champion's Lucky Dodge, Fortune's Path or save bonuses.~
@152 = ~Tymora's Blessing~

@155 = ~Lady's Grace~
@156 = ~Lady's Grace

Each time this ability is chosen, the Champion can use Lady's Favour one more time per day.~

@160 = ~Second Chance~
@161 = ~Second Chance

For 1 turn, any ally near the Champion who falls below 10% of their hit points is instantly healed to about half. Each ally can be saved once.~
@162 = ~A second chance!~

@165 = ~Lucky Break~
@166 = ~Lucky Break

Each time this ability is chosen, the Champion gains +5% resistance to physical damage, +5% resistance to magic damage and +5% magic resistance.~

@170 = ~Lucky Blow~
@171 = ~Lucky Blow

The dice favour the Champion's strikes. Each time this ability is chosen, its critical-hit range widens by 1: critical hits on 19–20 with one pick, and 18–20 with two.~

@180 = ~Tymora's Champions cannot use this item.~
